:"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a creature card is put into your graveyard during your main phase and the stack is empty, you have a chance to cast it before any player may attempt to remove that card from your graveyard.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple effects allow you to play a card from your graveyard, you must announce which permission you're using as you begin to play the card.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast one creature spell from your graveyard and then have a new Karador come under your control in the same turn, you may cast another creature spell from your graveyard that turn.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you begin to cast the spell, losing control of Karador won't affect the spell. You can finish casting it as normal.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you're paying, add any cost increases (such as the commander tax), then apply any cost reductions (such as that of Karador). The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must follow the normal timing permissions and restrictions of the spell you cast from your graveyard.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must pay the costs to cast that spell. If it has an alternative cost, you may cast it for that cost instead.","oracle_id":"304c194f-fa0b-42e5-93ca-8c587181d33c","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Geistlight Snare costs {2} less if you control a Spirit and an enchantment. It also costs {2} less if you control one permanent that's both an enchantment and a Spirit.","oracle_id":"45f159dc-a5f9-4335-896b-ad544c303801","published_at":"2021-11-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions (such as that of Mortality Spear). Mortality Spear's mana value is always 4, no matter what the total cost to cast it was.","oracle_id":"544acde0-850d-4c4f-8389-e22930d87345","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The mana value of this card is still 8, even if you only pay {W}{W} to cast it.","oracle_id":"e2f22cef-9494-4356-aa5c-619aecd7e74d","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
